# Muslim Rentals — Frontend environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# IMPORTANT — Next.js public env vars:
# Every variable below is prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, which means Next.js inlines
# its value into the client-side JavaScript bundle at build time. Anything
# placed in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable is visible to anyone who opens the site
# and views the bundled JS/network requests — it must NEVER hold a secret,
# API key, or credential. There are currently no server-only (non-public)
# environment variables read by this frontend's code.

# ─── API ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of the backend API (rentals/backend). Accepted with or without a
# trailing /api/v1 — src/lib/api.ts normalises either form.
# Used by: src/lib/api.ts
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# ─── Realtime ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of the Socket.IO server used for realtime features (e.g. messaging).
# Used by: src/lib/socket.ts
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=http://localhost:4000
